  riemann-at-home setup [--archive PATH]   download + verify + unpack the archive, install Lean + Mathlib cache
  riemann-at-home build [--gentle|--full]  start the official `lake build Main` in the background (or switch speed)
  riemann-at-home pause | resume | stop    control the running build (resumable: nothing compiled is lost)
  riemann-at-home status                   modules compiled, running or not, speed
  riemann-at-home record                   write a build record (rah/build/1) to ~/.riemann-at-home/records/
  riemann-at-home submit --repo DIR --dry-run   show how it opens / updates this computer's one PR (`gh`)
  riemann-at-home finish [--repo DIR]      done here: final record ("final": true), the bot merges the PR
  riemann-at-home name "NAME" | --anonymous | --clear   what the page shows instead of your GitHub login
  riemann-at-home page [--once] [--port N]  this computer's page at http://localhost:8642/
